// Convertible core - archive family: HFS+ file names to NFC UTF-8.
//
// HFS+ stores names as UTF-16 in (a variant of) Unicode canonical
// decomposition, so "\u00FC" is stored as "u" + U+0308. Users and every
// other archive format expect precomposed names, so readers recompose them.
// `compositions` lists every canonical pair composition of the Basic
// Multilingual Plane (base, combining mark -> composed character), excluding
// the composition exclusions; it is the Unicode Character Database's
// decomposition mapping (Unicode 16.0.0), extracted as data. Hangul
// syllables are composed arithmetically (Unicode chapter 3.12).
// Copyright (c) Convertible contributors. MIT licence; see LICENSE.
